34D. Allotment of agricultural lands consisting of more than one Khasra, the value of which exceeds Rs. 10,000/- (1) Where any land to which the Chapter applies has been leased to a displaced person and such land consists of more than one Khasra,
the aggregate value of which exceeds Rs. 10,000/- such portion of the land, the value of which does not exceed Rs. 10,000/- as the Regional Settlement Commissioner may select, shall be allotted to such person;
Provided that where any land or any part thereof has been sub-leased to a displaced person and the sub-lessee has been in occupation of that land or part thereof continuously from the first January, 1956, such land or part thereof, as the case may be, the value of which does not exceed Rs. 10,000/- as the Regional Settlement Commissioner may select, shall be allotted to such sub- lessee.

34E. Maximum area of land allotable under this Chapter- Notwithstanding any thing contained in the foregoing provisions of the rules - (a) no Khasra the value of which exceeds Rs.
10,000/- shall be allotted;
(b) the maximum area of land allotted to any one person shall not exceed Rs. 10,000/- in value. 34F.
